WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.008 --> 00:00:02.753
Hey, welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:06.747
This is Episode 100, so we're gonna try something special.

00:00:06.747 --> 00:00:07.930
Let me explain!

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.191
So, at the moment, we still use this gas, which is natural gas.

00:00:11.191 --> 00:00:14.171
But, it's a fossil fuel and we prefer to try something else.

00:00:15.282 --> 00:00:19.580
So I want to try to see if we can use
our food scraps to produce gas.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:25.592
For this, we're gonna prototype a biodigester,
and we have some friends coming over to help us out.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:28.639
But, first, we're gonna continue a little 
bit of work in our pig trailer!

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.719
We're gonna make the floor!

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.495
- In the previous videos, you saw us choose
and buy this pig trailer.

00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:38.031
We restored it and start building our new home.

00:00:38.546 --> 00:00:43.135
In the last update, we waterproofed it,
and now, it's time to put the floor.

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:46.119
We need to get some materials which we can reuse.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.255
- So, we're in a local scrapyard,
 and we found some plywood.

00:00:50.999 --> 00:00:54.624
Old plywood, but it's still in good condition.

00:00:56.077 --> 00:00:57.785
We will try to reuse it.

00:00:57.785 --> 00:01:01.519
We have also found some really cool insulation!

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:07.440
It's plastic-y, but I guess it still works.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.949
I like challenges.

00:01:45.053 --> 00:01:50.880
Go to the university, 
and you'll learn how to make all this.

00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:18.159
So, when we restored the trailer, we had to take 
some rotten wooden boards out of the sides.

00:02:18.679 --> 00:02:21.584
Apart from that, the rest is in quite good condition.

00:02:22.557 --> 00:02:27.385
Wouter is filling the gaps with wooden buttons
that we had left from the structure build.

00:02:27.385 --> 00:02:30.719
Next, we'll place the insulation that 
we found in the scrapyard.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.072
The first layer is in!

00:02:40.072 --> 00:02:41.760
Now, a second one.

00:02:50.119 --> 00:02:52.599
Then, it's time for the reused plywood boards.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.519
- The insulation is in, which was the green stuff you saw.

00:03:12.639 --> 00:03:16.679
Two layers, with on top a layer of multiplex.

00:03:17.818 --> 00:03:19.619
This is second hand multiplex.

00:03:19.619 --> 00:03:24.087
You can see little holes, and cracks.

00:03:25.235 --> 00:03:27.080
It's still usable as an underfloor.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.820
Now, we're going to tape the seams.

00:03:31.364 --> 00:03:38.083
Because, there is the biggest risk of air
 blowing in on a windy day...

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.291
And then, it's really not good for your insulation.

00:03:40.291 --> 00:03:41.280
So, this is something we want to tape.

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:46.136
And then, we can finish it with the foil taped on,
 and it's all nice and closed.

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:48.333
Cool! Let's start!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.320
- Okay, so, while Wouter is finishing that tape,
 I'm gonna start prepping a few boards here.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.345
We're gonna put the same basketball court on the floor again.

00:04:10.345 --> 00:04:14.295
There's a lot of dirt in the joints that we have to take out.

00:04:15.298 --> 00:04:21.744
And also, we have to cut out the ends,
which are filled with glue.

00:04:55.726 --> 00:04:56.525
Last piece!

00:05:07.151 --> 00:05:08.113
- That was it!

00:05:08.113 --> 00:05:10.198
Okay, that was it for this week on the pig trailer.

00:05:10.198 --> 00:05:11.320
We now have a nice floor.

00:05:11.679 --> 00:05:12.437
- You happy?

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:17.729
Nice basketball floor.

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:20.880
- So next, we're going to build our first prototype of a biodigester.

00:05:21.159 --> 00:05:23.429
But, I can imagine you don't know how it works.

00:05:23.429 --> 00:05:25.840
So, Adrian will first briefly explain what it actually is.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.096
- What's a biodigester?

00:05:28.611 --> 00:05:35.235
It's basically an airtight container, where we host bacteria 
that ferment organic matter without oxygen.

00:05:35.235 --> 00:05:38.266
We can feed it with food leftovers.

00:05:38.266 --> 00:05:41.315
Then, the bacteria do their magic, and after some days...

00:05:41.315 --> 00:05:46.239
We get methane we can use in a stove,
and liquid fertilizer for the plants.

00:05:47.039 --> 00:05:48.287
There are many types.

00:05:48.287 --> 00:05:50.744
Some quite big, even industrial scale.

00:05:50.744 --> 00:05:54.971
Some more DIY, underground, portable or automatized.

00:05:54.971 --> 00:05:58.226
What we want is a basic one, 
that we can build ourselves.

00:05:58.226 --> 00:06:02.280
To get a start with this technology,
 and see if it's interesting for us.

00:06:02.519 --> 00:06:04.709
Okay let's start on our bio digester.

00:06:04.709 --> 00:06:11.519
For this, we have the help of Fabio, who is coming from 
Instituto Favela de Paz, where he does incredible work.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:18.880
Instituto Favela de Paz is a project based in Sao Paulo,
Brazil in the favela of Jardim Angela.

00:06:19.199 --> 00:06:23.880
They promote a more peaceful living by 
developing educational projects around sustainability.

00:06:24.679 --> 00:06:28.531
engaging with the community through technology music and arts.

00:06:28.531 --> 00:06:35.570
Among many other projects, like recycled street lights, 
solar panels, technology workshops or urban gardening...

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:37.674
They also build biodigesters.

00:06:37.674 --> 00:06:42.480
As Fabio was visiting Portugal, we asked him 
to come andhelp us build our prototype.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.686
His designs are simple, not expensive and easy to replicate.

00:06:46.886 --> 00:06:48.102
He also brought some friends!

00:06:48.102 --> 00:06:50.453
Meet Gui, Lu and Jorge!

00:06:50.453 --> 00:06:53.167
They will assist us and help us with the building.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:58.117
First thing we need is an ICB container of 1000 liters.

00:06:58.604 --> 00:07:03.665
An ICB is a very common plastic
container used in many agricultural settings.

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:06.685
We found ours in a secondhand scrapyard.

00:07:08.478 --> 00:07:12.698
We will also need two barrels, 
with one slightly bigger than the other.

00:07:22.039 --> 00:07:24.860
Now, we need to paint it all black.

00:07:25.375 --> 00:07:32.027
Because, we need to avoid the sunlight to go in,
in order to not let the algae grow inside.

00:07:33.172 --> 00:07:39.320
So, the next step is disassembling this, paint the thing black, 
go back and then we can start the building.

00:07:50.199 --> 00:07:51.239
- Step two is cleaning.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.560
Step three: painting the primary layer.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:23.000
The next step is painting on the black!

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.925
I think it needs another layer after this.

00:08:36.925 --> 00:08:39.577
No light can peek through.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.837
All right! Now, it's completely black!

00:08:48.837 --> 00:08:50.760
We're gonna assemble it back together.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:00.820
- We have the ICB ready.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:03.000
Now, we need to prepare the blue barrels.

00:09:06.435 --> 00:09:10.601
We're gonna cut the top of this container,
 in order to put the other inside.

00:09:11.346 --> 00:09:14.305
So, I'm just gonna help them with that.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:49.654
Now, we are gonna make the hole for
the feeder.

00:09:49.654 --> 00:09:54.368
We will use this lid already that is well sealed underneath.

00:09:54.368 --> 00:10:00.321
So, it doesn't let the air go out, 
but we put the pipe in and we can feed it easily.

00:10:13.199 --> 00:10:15.399
Now, we are drilling the hole for some piping.

00:10:34.779 --> 00:10:37.601
This is gonna be the outlet of our biodigester.

00:10:37.601 --> 00:10:40.840
It's gonna bring the gas from the top of the tank.

00:10:41.479 --> 00:10:43.570
We have two exitpoints.

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:47.454
One will be to test the flame, to do tests basically.

00:10:47.855 --> 00:10:51.454
That's why it has a little tap.

00:10:51.454 --> 00:10:56.560
This will be the outlet for the gas that will go to our storage.

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:16.239
So, for all the connections in the top part of the biodigester, 
we are using rubber in order to make it airtight.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.292
This will be the mouth of our biodigester.

00:11:24.292 --> 00:11:30.280
So, we are gonna cut it here at 45 degrees, and put it inside.

00:11:51.159 --> 00:11:57.749
This is a 50 millimeter pipe that we are gonna cut,
and it's gonna be the for circuit of our biofertilizer.

00:11:57.749 --> 00:12:06.439
It will go to more or less the middle of the tank, 
go out another corner and then we will collect it outside.

00:12:22.319 --> 00:12:23.520
How is it going Fabio?

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:30.159
It will go to this bucket.

00:12:33.359 --> 00:12:35.817
Now, it's time to start with the gasometer

00:12:36.189 --> 00:12:42.740
It will consist in a tank that would be 
up and down storing our gas.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:47.399
And, creating the pressure that is needed 
to bring the gas to the stove.

00:12:48.239 --> 00:12:51.279
For the gasometer, we need to build some sort of a cage.

00:12:52.039 --> 00:12:56.119
So, when the barrel fills with the gas,
 it will go up, but not out.

00:14:26.199 --> 00:14:31.288
Now, we are going to install the inlet
 of the gas in our gasometer.

00:14:31.288 --> 00:14:33.520
And, the outlet that would go to our stove.

00:14:34.319 --> 00:14:40.640
We will put it a bit in the side, 
in order to avoid the cage to touch this piece.

00:14:52.159 --> 00:14:56.079
Okay! Now, it's time to build the cage!

00:15:12.479 --> 00:15:16.166
We now have the gasometer and the biodigester.

00:15:16.567 --> 00:15:20.081
We just need to connect it together.

00:15:25.039 --> 00:15:25.800
Here it is!

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:28.715
We finally put together all the pieces of the puzzle!

00:15:28.715 --> 00:15:32.720
And, our biodigesting system is ready to be fed and tested.

00:15:33.039 --> 00:15:35.439
Here is where our food scraps go in.

00:15:35.439 --> 00:15:38.520
This is where our biofertilizer will come out.

00:15:39.479 --> 00:15:42.560
And, here is where we can test the flame of the bio digester.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.796
This is our gasometer where we store our biogas.

00:15:48.254 --> 00:15:53.418
This is the place where the 
gas comes in and out to our stove.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.010
Now, it's time to feed it!

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:55.960
This is going to be fun.

00:15:56.479 --> 00:15:59.200
We were preparing a nice starter for a week already.

00:16:00.145 --> 00:16:02.035
Let me show you what it is!

00:16:05.399 --> 00:16:08.520
We went to see our neighbor Jorge
 to get some manure from his cows.

00:16:13.039 --> 00:16:15.920
We mix it with water and we left it 
to rest into the blue barrel.

00:16:23.399 --> 00:16:24.548
Now, we have it ready.

00:16:56.560 --> 00:17:04.159
Now, we are filling it up with water, until we seal this pipe,
that gets to more or less half of the container.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:07.279
Now, we are going to put some bacteria 'hotels'.

00:17:07.279 --> 00:17:12.159
They are going tofloat and increase 
the surface where they can live.

00:17:15.079 --> 00:17:16.960
So, the bacteria can stick to that.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:51.439
Now, the last step is to put water in between both barrels,
in order to seal the gas in the top one.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:58.039
We finished our biodigester!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.600
Now, we need to move it to
its final location, in the blue tent.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:08.279
We couldn't do this before, because Kevin was 
still renovating it, as you have seen in Update 96.

00:18:18.039 --> 00:18:20.520
So, now, we need to move a lot of heavy liquid poop.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:21.439
Great...

00:18:22.199 --> 00:18:24.880
Luckily, Jorge came to help us out with his tractor.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.667
- Alright, so, here we have it!

00:18:52.667 --> 00:18:54.479
The final prototype of the bio digester!

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:58.280
Unfortunately, there is no big flame yet, or gas being produced...

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.920
Because, it takes a while before the bacteria do that.

00:19:01.399 --> 00:19:05.640
And, it probably also requires some tweaking from our side
 tofind the right temperature and pH level.

00:19:06.279 --> 00:19:10.079
But, you can find more of that in the research module,
 where we will continue to post updates.

00:19:11.479 --> 00:19:14.595
Or, subscribe on YouTube and see how it's going to go.

00:19:14.595 --> 00:19:18.780
Because, we're probably also going to make some upgrades
 to the whole system of installing a shredder.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:20.520
That makes it easier for the food to go in!

00:19:21.319 --> 00:19:23.600
Yeah, so, this is not the last time you've seen this guy.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.520
But, for now, it's time to move on,
because it's grape-picking time.

00:19:28.479 --> 00:19:32.312
It's that time of the year where it's time to harvest the grapes,
 and we're going to help out the neighbors.

00:19:32.312 --> 00:19:37.239
And, I'm also going to introduce you to a new lady,
that you might have already seen in the previous videos!

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:41.960
But now, she's going to join us in 
actually picking all the grapes.

00:19:42.439 --> 00:19:43.079
Let's go!

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:45.199
- Hello, my name's Ingrid!

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:49.439
I'm half Dutch, half English and I consider 
myself to be the granny of the group.

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:59.464
You'll often find me in my pajamas doing some cross stitch, baking bread, 
sneaking biscuits from the kitchen, or reading by the lagoon.

00:20:00.039 --> 00:20:04.560
Before coming to Project Kamp, I was working at YouTube
and finishing my masters in AI-ethics.

00:20:05.079 --> 00:20:09.309
My passion is helping people disconnect from technology,
 and reconnect with nature.

00:20:09.309 --> 00:20:15.393
Which, is why I decided to get out from behind my desk, 
turn away from my screen and head off to Portugal!

00:20:15.393 --> 00:20:16.960
To chop trees and get my hands dirty!

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.399
Okay, now, we can go grape picking!

00:20:24.359 --> 00:20:31.279
So, today, a bunch of us are heading over to our neighbors,
Antonio and Fernanda, as they need a couple extra hands picking grapes.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:33.159
This over here is their field.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:35.319
A bunch of the team is already out there.

00:20:36.119 --> 00:20:37.439
So, let's see if we can help!

00:20:40.884 --> 00:20:42.600
Perfect! Tincho, how can I help?

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:47.039
- You can grab these buckets, and some clippers there.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:07.439
Kevin and Alice, have you gone grape picking before?

00:21:08.159 --> 00:21:09.279
- This is the first time.

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:10.560
How is it?

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:14.520
Wow!

00:21:15.319 --> 00:21:16.079
- Yeah, it's good!

00:21:18.292 --> 00:21:19.052
Tasty?

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:20.439
Very sweet.

00:21:40.687 --> 00:21:42.166
- It already looks beautiful.

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:47.359
It's nice.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:48.880
You want to have one?

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:50.079
- Please!

00:21:51.039 --> 00:21:54.920
Dorian, if you can take some of these grapes home, 
is there anything you can make with them?

00:21:56.399 --> 00:21:58.720
I would flavor some Kombucha with it.

00:22:00.287 --> 00:22:03.287
You can make some wine,
but I don't have the tools for it...

00:22:29.119 --> 00:22:30.720
Antonio turned 70 today.

00:22:32.439 --> 00:22:34.720
He was just saying
the secrets of staying fit.

00:22:35.119 --> 00:22:36.359
- Ah, grape picking!

00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:37.520
Is that the secret?

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:38.199
- Yes.

00:22:38.199 --> 00:22:39.119
Keeping on working.

00:23:08.075 --> 00:23:10.354
Chester has discovered the fallen grape.

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:12.840
Are they tasty, Chester?

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:15.159
Okay, that's it for this afternoon.

00:23:15.399 --> 00:23:19.760
We spent three hours with 13 people,
picking all of the grapes here in the vineyard.

00:23:20.720 --> 00:23:23.560
And, we have loaded up the truck
three times full of buckets of grapes.

00:23:24.039 --> 00:23:26.399
So, now, it is time to go and enjoy some wine.

00:24:41.640 --> 00:24:45.039
This is where they leave the wine now for five days.

00:25:02.119 --> 00:25:07.279
- All right, so, after that celebration we actually have another one,
 because this is a special video -- number 100!

00:25:07.880 --> 00:25:10.239
It took over three years
to actually get to this point.

00:25:10.239 --> 00:25:15.161
Many videos uploaded, many people came to help out,
and also all of you guys!

00:25:15.161 --> 00:25:16.760
Thanks for watching and making this possible!

00:25:17.319 --> 00:25:19.079
So, now, a little toast with Antonio's wine.

00:25:29.159 --> 00:25:31.159
All right, so, that was it for this video!

00:25:31.439 --> 00:25:32.902
If you already want to see the next one...

00:25:32.902 --> 00:25:36.268
Where we're going to install a new solar system,
 and continue working on the pig trailer...

00:25:36.268 --> 00:25:39.003
Make sure to subscribe and support on Patreon!

00:25:39.003 --> 00:25:43.908
You can then already see the next video 
one week ahead, in 4K without advertisements.

00:25:44.452 --> 00:25:47.420
Or not, just subscribe and you can see it next week!

00:25:47.420 --> 00:25:48.508
Same channel, same time.

00:25:49.138 --> 00:25:50.492
Thank you for watching!

00:25:51.093 --> 00:25:52.991
Here's to 200 videos!

